  "caveats": [
    "Bach, Pope, Liou & Batelaan (2013) Fig. 3e images the central five diffraction orders through an electrostatic quadrupole zoom lens without an independent screen-angle calibration bar and compiles 6,235 single-electron hits via finite-size blob localization (elevating trough minima to 0.24-0.49). In simulators/double_slit_simulator.html, BACH_DATA stores horizontal coordinates with a 5x scale factor (+/-2.5584 instead of +/-0.51168 mrad). No visibility, background, slit-geometry, or q parameter is fitted here: parameter-free exterior q_local(y) -> 1 matches q = 1 Fraunhofer to < 1.9e-5 pointwise, whereas naive uniform exterior q = q0 shifts m = +-2 fringes by +11.00% and lifts the magnification-invariant m = +-2 sinc^2 envelope from 0.6448 to 0.7042."
  ],
